[; Evaluate an RPN expression by folding over the token sequence, carrying the
   stack as a DOCUMENT ([stack [n …] [n …]]) rather than an opaque list — so the
   intermediate state is inspectable data at every step.
   3 4 + 5 * = 35.
   Rewritten for the v0.8.0 surface (RULED: VC-28); the original was pre-reshape
   (`:using`/`:init`/`:case`/`:yield` colon clauses, `[?fn ($a, $b)]` comma
   params, `nth(x, 1)` call-parens).

   R-A1 migration (2026-08-25, the Cluster A settlement): a node-set placed in
   element content is spliced — `[?splice $acc/*]` pushes the existing stack
   items as direct children — so the child axis reads the stack and the former
   descendant-axis workaround (#961) is retired. `$acc/*` (not `$acc/n`) feeds
   the push because a wildcard read never field-collapses; `$acc/n` reads are
   fine as operands (a one-item field collapses to its scalar, which arithmetic
   accepts; a multi-item match stays a node-set, which `$nth` indexes). ]
[?reduce (3, 4, :plus, 5, :times)
  [using [?fn ($acc $tok)
    [?match $tok
      [case :plus [stack [n [+ [$nth $acc/n 1] [$nth $acc/n 2]]]]]
      [case :times [stack [n [* [$nth $acc/n 1] [$nth $acc/n 2]]]]]
      [else [stack [n $tok] [?splice $acc/*]]]]]]
  [init [stack]]]
